# WebSocket commands — use a WS client connected to:
# ws://{{host}}/ws?token={{authToken}}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/ws
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  ## The RØDECaster's own SD / USB recorder

  This is the recorder inside the desk, NOT Metocast's FLAC recording of its USB audio (see
  "RØDECaster - Audio Recording").

  ```json
  { "type": "rodecaster.record.start" }
  { "type": "rodecaster.record.stop" }
  ```

  Each replies `{ "type": "ok" }`, or `{ "type": "error", "message": "rodecaster_not_connected" }`,
  or `rodecaster_no_media` when a start finds no SD card or USB drive. The desk's own report arrives
  to every client, and on connect while the desk is connected, as:

  ```json
  { "type": "rodecaster.record.state", "state": { "status": "recording", "mediaPresent": true } }
  ```

  `status` is `stopped`, `paused` or `recording`. A start while paused resumes.

  For the hardware check, `rcast record status` and `rcast record start|stop` (in the `rodecaster`
  crate) read and drive the same recorder from a terminal.
}
